# /pubspec.lock  (committed on purpose; see the note below)
# pubspec.lock IS committed. This is an application, not a package, and Dart's
# own guidance is to commit the lockfile for apps so every build resolves to the
# same versions. Ignoring it meant CI resolved dependencies fresh on every run:
# `html` 0.15.7 was published on 2026-08-28 and broke the transitive
# flutter_html, so the reader build failed in CI while succeeding locally on the
# 0.15.6 my lockfile had. Committing it makes "works locally" mean something.
# **/pubspec.lock

